course: dictionary
lesson: 2983
title: Duckling and the ugly duckling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A duckling is a baby duck, just as a kitten is a baby cat. «A mother duck and her ducklings» crossed the park, so the mother is the grown-up duck and the ducklings are the babies following her.
explain: Some words also have a second meaning in stories. In «The Ugly Duckling», a young bird looks plain and awkward at first. An «ugly duckling» is someone who seems plain or odd when young but grows up to be beautiful or great.
explain: Check the clues around the word. If the sentence is about a pond, a nest or swimming, it means a real baby duck. If it is about a person who looks awkward and then changes, it means the story meaning. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: A duckling is a baby duck.
fact: Ducklings hatch from eggs, then follow their mother and grow feathers.
fact: Ducklings follow the first moving thing they see after hatching, usually their mother; this is called imprinting.
fact: «An ugly duckling» means someone who seems plain or awkward at first but grows up to be beautiful or great.
fact: The plural of duckling is ducklings, as in «fluffy ducklings».
exercise: «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» How many ducklings did Ella rescue? | *Six | Ten | Four | Nine
exercise: «In spring a mallard mother marches a wobbly line of ducklings across the path.» What is a duckling? | *A baby duck | A type of swan | A grown-up duck with a green head | A nest on the water
exercise: Mia reads that someone is «an ugly duckling». What does this mean in a story? | A person who is unkind and rude | A person who is really a duck | *Someone who seems plain at first but grows up to be great | Someone who is always asleep
test: What do ducklings usually follow first after they hatch? | A loud noise | A piece of bread | *Their mother | A pond
test: At the park, which food is much better to give ducklings than bread? | *Oats | Crisps | Sweets | Cake
exam: In «Ducklings follow the first moving thing they see after hatching», what does hatching mean? | Flying high over the water | *Coming out of an egg | Swimming away from the nest | Growing feathers
